cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "npcadd: a reproducible computational pipeline for natural-product drug discovery"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata, and also cite
  the underlying scientific tools listed under references below — they did the
  scientific work.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "npcadd contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/shafi22211091095-droid/cursor-ai"
abstract: >-
  npcadd is a pip-installable, fully configuration-driven pipeline that takes a
  GC-MS-derived phytochemical set from SMILES to a validated, ranked,
  publication-ready result. It enforces a mandatory docking-validation gate
  (co-crystal redocking with in-place RMSD, property-matched decoy enrichment,
  and a random-ligand null distribution) before any screening runs, and it
  refuses to rank compounds by raw docking affinity because that score scales
  with molecular size. Every run records complete provenance: git commit,
  configuration hash, SHA256 of every input and output, resolved package
  versions, platform, and all random seeds. No GUI tool appears in the critical
  path.
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - molecular docking
  - natural products
  - virtual screening
  - ADMET
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
